 ## Overview
-Dynamic and Spacetime Modeling extends static 3D Gaussian Splatting to handle temporal variations, enabling real-time novel view synthesis for dynamic scenes . It solves the problem of modeling emerging, vanishing, and deforming content by integrating time-dependent attributes (motion, opacity, rotation) into the Gaussian representation . It is distinguished from static methods by its explicit handling of time as a dimension, using either learned deformation fields or parametric polynomial trajectories to model geometry changes .
+Dynamic and Spacetime Modeling extends static 3D Gaussian Splatting to handle temporal variations, enabling real-time novel view synthesis for dynamic scenes [G]. It solves the problem of modeling emerging, vanishing, and deforming content by integrating time-dependent attributes (motion, opacity, rotation) into the Gaussian representation [G]. It is distinguished from static methods and siblings like [Deformable 3D Gaussians](16260-deformable-3d-gaussians.md) and [Spacetime Gaussian Feature Splatting](16313-spacetime-gaussian-feature-splatting.md) by its explicit handling of time as a dimension, using either learned deformation fields or parametric polynomial trajectories to model geometry changes [G].
 
